          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ജിജ്ഞാസ — jijñāsa — \"curiosity\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കുട്ടികൾക്ക് എല്ലാ കാര്യത്തിലും ജിജ്ഞാസയുണ്ട്. kuṭṭikaḷkkŭ ellā kāryattiluṁ jijñāsayuṇṭŭ. Children are curious about everything."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What one is curious about takes -ഇൽ. The adjective is ജിജ്ഞാസയുള്ള, curious."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ജിജ്ഞാസ (jijñāsa) is borrowed from Sanskrit jijñāsā, \"the wish to know\" (Monier-Williams), the wish-form of the root jñā, \"to know\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
