          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഉന്മേഷം — unmēṣaṁ — \"freshness; vigour\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "രാവിലെ ഒരു ചായ കുടിച്ചാൽ എനിക്ക് ഉന്മേഷം കിട്ടും. rāvile oru cāya kuṭiccāl enikkŭ unmēṣaṁ kiṭṭuṁ. If I drink a tea in the morning, I feel fresh."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The fresh, wide-awake feeling after rest or a bath: കുളി കഴിഞ്ഞ് ഉന്മേഷം (unmēṣaṁ) തോന്നി."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഉന്മേഷം (unmēṣaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit unmeṣa, \"the opening of the eyes\" (Monier-Williams). Malayalam took it for the feeling of being wide awake and fresh."
            }
          ]
        },
